  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive an integer array `nums`.\n\n* The **low** score of `nums` is the **smallest** absolute difference between any two integers.\n* The **high** score of `nums` is the **largest** absolute difference between any two integers.\n* The **score** of `nums` is the sum of the **high** and **low** scores.\n\nOutput the **smallest score** after **changing two elements** of `nums`.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,4,7,8,5]\n\n**Output:** 3\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n* Change `nums[0]` and `nums[1]` to be 6 so that `nums` becomes [6,6,7,8,5].\n* The low score is the smallest absolute difference: |6 - 6| = 0.\n* The high score is the largest absolute difference: |8 - 5| = 3.\n* The sum of high and low score is 3.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,4,3]\n\n**Output:** 0\n\n**Explanation:**\n\n* Change `nums[1]` and `nums[2]` to 1 so that `nums` becomes [1,1,1].\n* The sum of largest absolute difference and smallest absolute difference is 0.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `3 <= nums.length <= 105`\n* `1 <= nums[i] <= 109`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
